package Libraries.Game.Graphics.Trees

use Libraries.Game.BoundingBox
use Libraries.Containers.Array
use Libraries.Interface.Item3D

/*
RenderTreePart3D is one half of a StaticDynamicRenderTree3D: the static half
or the dynamic half. It holds leaves, one for each item, and finds the ones
inside a view, a box or a sphere. The leaves belong to the render tree, which
moves them between its two halves.

This class has blank actions. Each kind of render tree uses a different
kind of part:

- RenderBoundingVolumeTree3D, a tree of boxes, for DynamicVolumeRenderTree3D.
- RenderCellTree3D, a grid of cells that splits into smaller cells, for
  QuadTree3D and Octree3D.

Every part has a margin, kept here. The box calculations a part needs, such
as giving a leaf its box with the margin, are actions on the leaf,
RenderTreeNode3D.

Attribute: Example

use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Trees.RenderTreePart3D
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Trees.RenderBoundingVolumeTree3D

RenderBoundingVolumeTree3D volumes
RenderTreePart3D part = volumes
part:SetMargin(0.25)
output part:GetMargin()
*/
class RenderTreePart3D
    // How much bigger than its item a leaf's box is made, on every side.
    number margin = 0

    /*
    This action sets how much bigger than its item a leaf's box is made, on
    every side. A bigger margin means fewer changes as items move, but more
    items found just outside a view.

    Attribute: Parameter value The margin.
    */
    action SetMargin(number value)
        margin = value
    end

    /*
    This action returns how much bigger than its item a leaf's box is made.

    Attribute: Returns The margin.
    */
    action GetMargin returns number
        return margin
    end

    /*
    This action returns how many leaves the part holds.

    Attribute: Returns The number of leaves.
    */
    action GetSize returns integer
        return 0
    end

    /*
    This action returns how many levels the part has below its top, or -1
    when it is empty. What a level is depends on the kind of part.

    Attribute: Returns The number of levels.
    */
    action GetHeight returns integer
        return -1
    end

    /*
    This action adds a leaf, with a box around the given bounds of its item.

    Attribute: Parameter leaf The leaf to add.
    Attribute: Parameter itemBounds The item's bounds in the world.
    */
    action Add(RenderTreeNode3D leaf, BoundingBox itemBounds)
    end

    /*
    This action removes a leaf. The leaf itself is not reused, since it
    belongs to the render tree.

    Attribute: Parameter leaf The leaf to remove.
    */
    action Remove(RenderTreeNode3D leaf)
    end

    /*
    This action updates a leaf whose item has moved.

    Attribute: Parameter leaf The leaf whose item moved.
    Attribute: Parameter itemBounds The item's new bounds in the world.
    Attribute: Returns True if the leaf changed place in the part.
    */
    action Move(RenderTreeNode3D leaf, BoundingBox itemBounds) returns boolean
        return false
    end

    /*
    This action removes every leaf. The leaves themselves are not changed.
    */
    action Empty
    end

    /*
    This action adds to the result every item whose box is at least partly
    inside the volume. The result decides which of its lists each item goes
    in, and skips items it already has.

    Attribute: Parameter volume The volume, such as a camera's view or a
    light's shadow column.
    Attribute: Parameter result The result to add the items to.
    */
    action Collect(CullingVolume3D volume, RenderTree3DResult result)
    end

    /*
    This action adds to the results every item whose box overlaps the box.

    Attribute: Parameter box The box, in world coordinates.
    Attribute: Parameter results The array to add the items to.
    */
    action Collect(BoundingBox box, Array<Item3D> results)
    end

    /*
    This action adds to the results every item whose box overlaps the sphere
    with the given center and radius.

    Attribute: Parameter x The x coordinate of the sphere's center.
    Attribute: Parameter y The y coordinate of the sphere's center.
    Attribute: Parameter z The z coordinate of the sphere's center.
    Attribute: Parameter radius The sphere's radius.
    Attribute: Parameter results The array to add the items to.
    */
    action Collect(number x, number y, number z, number radius, Array<Item3D> results)
    end

    /*
    This action adds to the result every item whose box overlaps the sphere
    with the given center and radius, such as a point light's reach. The
    result decides which of its lists each item goes in, and skips items it
    already has.

    Attribute: Parameter x The x coordinate of the sphere's center.
    Attribute: Parameter y The y coordinate of the sphere's center.
    Attribute: Parameter z The z coordinate of the sphere's center.
    Attribute: Parameter radius The sphere's radius.
    Attribute: Parameter result The result to add the items to.
    */
    action Collect(number x, number y, number z, number radius, RenderTree3DResult result)
    end

    /*
    This action returns the first leaf in the part's own order, or undefined
    when the part is empty. With GetNextLeaf, it visits every leaf once. The
    order depends on how the part is built, not on when leaves were added.

    Attribute: Returns The first leaf, or undefined.
    */
    action GetFirstLeaf returns RenderTreeNode3D
        return undefined
    end

    /*
    This action returns the leaf after the given one in the part's own
    order, or undefined after the last leaf. It finds it by following the
    links between the part's nodes, so it takes a few steps however many
    leaves there are, and it makes no new objects. A leaf that is no longer
    in the part has no leaf after it.

    Attribute: Parameter leaf A leaf in this part.
    Attribute: Returns The next leaf, or undefined.
    */
    action GetNextLeaf(RenderTreeNode3D leaf) returns RenderTreeNode3D
        return undefined
    end
end
